AUTODOC audio.doc — W1 backend graph API (Task 6 signatures, Task 14 docs).
Header: audio_io/audio.h. Engine/device geometry: RI_AUDIO_SR 48000,
RI_AUDIO_BLOCK 64 (LOCKED, spec 2.3), RI_DEVICE_FRAMES 256 (hypothesis
until M1.1). Missing AHI prints RI_AUDIO_NULL_MSG and runs the null
backend (offline render only).

struct AudioObject *AuCreateObject(struct Library *AudioBase, struct TagItem *tags)
  Create the graph object. Inputs: library base + tags. Result: object or NULL.

uint32_t AuAddSource(struct AudioObject *ao, struct TagItem *tags)
  Add a song source (AUTA_SongPath tag). Result: source id.

uint32_t AuAddBus(struct AudioObject *ao, const char *name, struct TagItem *tags)
  Add a named bus. Result: bus id.

int AuConnect(struct AudioObject *ao, uint32_t src, uint32_t bus)
  Wire source to bus. Result: 0 ok, nonzero bad id.

int AuStart(struct AudioObject *ao)
  Start the render task (null backend on host). Result: 0 ok.

void AuStop(struct AudioObject *ao)
  Stop the render task. No result.

uint32_t AuQueryAttr(struct AudioObject *ao, uint32_t attr)
  Query AUQA_LatencyFrames / AUQA_XRUN_COUNT. Result: attribute value.

int AuRenderToFile(struct AudioObject *ao, const char *path, uint32_t ms)
  Offline render ms milliseconds to a 16-bit mono WAV. Result: 0 ok.

Extras (NOT frozen): AuBackendName, AuDumpEvents, au_render_frames,
au_rewind, au_render_song_to_wav, au_null_render_to_wav — see header.
